    {
      "id": "a0",
      "pos": 1,
      "text": "The U.S. Census Bureau reports that women's median annual earnings for full-time, year-round work were about 84 percent of men's in 2022.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "pos": 2,
      "text": "Men and women in the United States labor market are distributed unevenly across occupations and industries.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "pos": 3,
      "text": "Some employers pay lower wages to women than to equally productive men.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "Blau and Kahn's 2017 Journal of Economic Literature survey decomposed the gender wage gap using Oaxaca-Blinder techniques.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "Blau and Kahn concluded that measured differences in education and work experience fully account for the gender wage gap.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "pos": 6,
      "text": "Blau and Kahn found that occupational and industry differences accounted for roughly half of the explained portion of the gender wage gap.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "pos": 7,
      "text": "The unexplained residual accounted for about 38 percent of the gender wage gap in 2010.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "pos": 8,
      "text": "Roughly 38 percent of the 2010 gender pay differential remained unaccounted for by measured worker and job characteristics.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "pos": 9,
      "text": "Claudia Goldin's 2014 American Economic Association presidential address attributed the remaining gap largely to nonlinear returns to long and inflexible work hours.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9",
      "pos": 10,
      "text": "Bertrand, Goldin, and Katz found that the earnings gap among University of Chicago MBA graduates widened in the years following graduation.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
